  "id": "dosedconfused",
  "neon": "#4fd39a",
  "note": "A chemist on the corner where Foundry Way meets the Gate Road. A green cross over the door that flickers on the downstroke, a night hatch beside it with a bell, and a window full of boxes that have faded down one side from standing in the light. Three floors, and the dispensing counter is up a step.\n\nIt was a flat box with a small dark sign on it. A chemist is a SHOPFRONT with rooms over it, so it has the stack the rest of the street has: a stone plinth, a glazed podium under a canopy that reaches the kerb, a cornice, then a set-back shaft in the shop's own green-grey. Three palettes, because the setbacks were there and a single tone made four storeys read as one lump - the same thing adequate.json records.\n\nThe oriel on the left is the dispensary, which is the room that wants the light and is the one part of the frontage a chemist would pay to project.\n\nThe roof sign is the HATCH and not the name. The fascia already says the name; a roof board repeating it tells a player nothing, and the hatch is the thing worth knowing about at three in the morning.",
